  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Threshold sits between 2 V and 4 V (3 V typ) at 90 µA and falls as the junction warms: near 1.9 V typ at 150 °C for 90 µA (Diagram 10). On-resistance is guaranteed at 10 V of gate drive; typical curves also cover 4.5 V, 5 V and 7 V; at 4.5 V the resistance turns sharply upward near 16 A and at 5 V near 44 A (Diagram 6). The gate is rated ±20 V and leaks 100 nA at most at 20 V. Charging the gate from 0 to 10 V takes 22 nC typ with the drain switching 100 V at 18 A; the Miller plateau sits near 4.4 V. Internal gate resistance is 2.5 Ω typ."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate charge",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "The charge figures are spans of the VGS-against-charge trace. Qg(th) runs from zero to the point where VGS reaches the threshold; Qgs runs from zero to the start of the flat plateau; Qgd is the width of the plateau; Qsw runs from Qg(th) to the end of the plateau; Qg is the whole charge up to the stated gate voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "On-resistance at 36 A and 10 V rises with junction temperature, to about 67 mΩ typ and 78 mΩ max at 150 °C (Diagram 9). The minimum breakdown voltage rises from about 187 V at -55 °C to about 221 V at 150 °C (Diagram 15). Drain leakage at 160 V grows from 1 µA max at 25 °C to 100 µA max at 125 °C. The current and power ratings fall to zero as the case approaches 150 °C (Diagrams 1 and 2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Junction-to-case resistance is 1 K/W max. To ambient it is 75 K/W on a minimal footprint and 50 K/W with 6 cm² of copper on the drain. The 125 W dissipation rating assumes the case held at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The intrinsic diode carries 36 A continuous and 144 A pulsed with the case at 25 °C, drops 0.9 V typ and 1.2 V max at 36 A, and recovers in 105 ns typ with 429 nC typ of charge when commutated at 100 A/µs from 18 A against 100 V. The reverse diode dv/dt rating is 10 kV/µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 9,
